<article class="env-remark" id="0GBE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GBE">Remark <span data-tag="0GBE">87.21.8</span> <span class="named">(Variant for adic-star)</span>.</a>  Let $P$ be a local property of morphisms of $\textit{WAdm}^{adic*}$, see Remark <a href="/tag/0ANH" data-tag="0ANH">87.21.4</a>. We say $P$ is <em>stable under base change</em> if given $B \to A$ and $B \to C$ in $\textit{WAdm}^{adic*}$ we have $P(B \to A) \Rightarrow P(C \to A \widehat{\otimes }_ B C)$. This makes sense as $A \widehat{\otimes }_ B C$ is an object of $\textit{WAdm}^{adic*}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0GB4" data-tag="0GB4">87.4.12</a>. In exactly the same way we obtain a variant of Lemma <a href="/tag/0GBD" data-tag="0GBD">87.21.7</a> for morphisms between locally adic* formal algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
</article>